{"duration_api_ms":5140,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"1b386a81-0c03-4909-9dfd-7100cf4f0711","total_cost_usd":0.0132705,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":629,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":405,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":21},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":629,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":405,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":629,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":629},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1195,"outputTokens":22,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.00013050000000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":405,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":629,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.013139999999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":21,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":629,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**The creation/redemption arbitrage mechanism** keeps them aligned.\n\n**How it works:**\n- **Authorized Participants (APs)**, typically large broker-dealers, can create or redeem ETF shares directly with the issuer in large blocks (\"creation units,\" often 10,000–50,000 shares).\n- **Premium (price > NAV):** APs buy the underlying securities, deliver them to the issuer for new ETF shares, and sell those shares on the exchange. This adds supply and pushes the price down.\n- **Discount (price < NAV):** APs buy cheap ETF shares, redeem them for the underlying basket, and sell the basket. This reduces supply and lifts the price.\n\n**Supporting factors:**\n- **Intraday transparency.** Daily holdings disclosure and real-time iNAV estimates let market makers price fair value.\n- **Competitive market makers** narrow spreads.\n- **Liquid underlying assets** make arbitrage cheap and fast.\n\n**When it weakens:** For illiquid holdings (high-yield bonds, frontier markets), during market stress, or when underlying markets are closed, premiums and discounts can widen.","ttft_ms":1371,"type":"result","duration_ms":4635,"uuid":"79bd9eef-7276-4fab-bc75-2c4a6875295d","ttft_stream_ms":1142,"time_to_request_ms":69,"first_content_frame_ms":1142,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
